  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "the rave-to-big-beat break at the fast end (the Prodigy's early records, around 135-150): a sped-up Amen-derived break over a driving kick, eighth hats and a held rave bass",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: the Amen's first bar with a four under it, then its chopped answer with a roll into the bar line; eighth hats; the sub held on the root and stepping down at the phrase. 135-150 is above the fast band's 130 and below drum and bass's 160, so it plays at 130 under the Breaks spell."
  }
